# {{APP_NAME}}

JNative mobile project (template). Shared WASM core + thin Android/iOS shells.

## Identifiers

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Android applicationId | `{{ANDROID_APPLICATION_ID}}` |
| iOS bundle id | `{{IOS_BUNDLE_ID}}` |
| Version / build | `{{VERSION}}` / `{{BUILD_NUMBER}}` |

Configured in `jnative.toml` `[mobile]` — applied into platform projects on each `jnative mobile build`.

## Commands

```bash
jnative doctor --mobile
jnative mobile build --target web
jnative mobile build --target android
jnative mobile build --target ios
jnative mobile devices --target android
jnative mobile devices --target ios
jnative mobile run --target android --device <id>
jnative mobile run --target ios --device <id>
jnative mobile logs --target android --device <id>
```

Serve web dist:

```bash
jnative mobile build --target web
cd dist && python3 -m http.server 8765
```

## Limits

- Debug builds / iOS Simulator only this round (no store signing).
- KV storage is ordinary preferences — not for secrets.
- WASM in WebView is not auto-debugged via LLDB; use compile diagnostics, JS console, bridge errors, and platform logs.
- Generator never overwrites existing files; regenerating the template will skip user-modified native sources.
